{"id":"8234d253-8a3f-4253-ae8a-1e60a6f5928c","object":"chat.completion","created":1784962291,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case['nodes']\\n    core_distance = case['core_distance']\\n    distances = case['distances']\\n    \\n    # Build edges with mutual reachability\\n    edges = []\\n    for u, v, d in distances:\\n        core_u = core_distance[u]\\n        core_v = core_distance[v]\\n        weight = max(core_u, core_v, d)\\n        # canonicalize: ensure u < v as strings\\n        if u > v:\\n            u, v = v, u\\n        edges.append((weight, u, v))\\n    \\n    # Sort by (weight, u, v) for deterministic tie-breaking\\n    edges.sort()\\n    \\n    # Union-Find\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    def find(x):\\n        while parent[x] != x:\\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\\n            x = parent[x]\\n        return x\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        # rank heuristic: simply attach ry under rx (no rank needed for determinism)\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        return True\\n    \\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    for weight, u, v in edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, weight])\\n            total_weight += weight\\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\\n                break\\n    \\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Graph is disconnected')\\n    \\n    return {\\n        'mst_edges': mst_edges,\\n        'total_weight': total_weight\\n    }\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to generate Python code for solve(case) that implements mutual-reachability MST as described. The payload has nodes, core_distance dict, distances list of [node1, node2, distance]. For each pair, compute mutual reachability = max(core_distance[node1], core_distance[node2], distance). Then build graph and find MST using Kruskal's algorithm with union-find. Must handle tie-breaking: first by weight (mutual reachability), then by endpoint IDs (presumably alphabetically? The instruction says \"Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs.\" So sort edges by (weight, node1, node2) where node1 < node2 (canonicalize undirected endpoints). Then run Kruskal until n-1 edges. Return mst_edges (list of [node1, node2, weight]) and total_weight (sum). If graph is disconnected, raise ValueError. Use only standard library. Ensure deterministic union-find.\n\nImplementation details: \n- Parse case dict.\n- nodes list.\n- Build adjacency: for each distance triplet (u,v,d), compute core_u, core_v, weight = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], d). Canonicalize: ensure u < v (string compare) to avoid duplicates.\n- Collect all edges: list of (weight, u, v).\n- Sort edges: sort by (weight, u, v).\n- Union-Find: parent dict, rank dict.\n- mst_edges = [], total = 0.\n- For each edge in sorted edges: find roots, if different, union, add [u, v, weight] to mst_edges, total += weight.\n- After loop, if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes)-1: raise ValueError(\"disconnected\").\n- Return {\"mst_edges\": mst_edges, \"total_weight\": total}.\n\nEdge cases: nodes may not be sorted; ensure canonical u < v using string comparison. Use node names as strings.\n\nThe output schema requires mst_edges array where each item is [string, string, number]. OK.\n\nWe must output the implementation as a JSON string within an object with key \"implementation\". The entire response must be that JSON object.\n\nSo final response: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case): ...\"} with proper JSON escaping.\n\nLet's write the function. Ensure no imports beyond standard library. Use typing? Not needed. Use simple data structures.\n\nWe'll produce the Python source as a single string with newlines escaped.\n\nLet's write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"pro